he direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to one decimal place where appropriate." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =6\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{134}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =42\\cdot (0.719\\,33…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(30.212\\,27…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈30.2n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82f31c6e-f9df-5e0a-88a4-a8ccfca00258" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "036fc6a1-1cc2-5e3e-8339-2a5e9600ad42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286563} {:answer/id #uuid "aff92055-0915-5b24-8b95-c93c9ba8c1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286564} {:answer/id #uuid "1023b97a-e803-5748-b4f6-b1a6cda7279c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286565} {:answer/id #uuid "105f0a84-aaa5-59e1-af58-7552dd8584b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286566} {:answer/id #uuid "b05e6234-3743-5034-a1fd-c1aebcc900cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "105f0a84-aaa5-59e1-af58-7552dd8584b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286566} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f1437eb-18f3-5c23-85c2-e6683d19ba5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "936b6abc-9399-5bd0-a7d7-a2d952f190b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-146304" :question/problem "The vector $u$ has magnitude $2,$ the vector $v$ has magnitude $5,$ and the angle between the vectors is ${0}^{∘}.$ What is $u\\times v?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $u$ and $v$ are nonzero vectors. Then, $u\\times v=0$ if and only if $u∥v.$\n\nSince the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${0}^{∘},$ our vectors must be parallel. \n\nTherefore, $u\\times v=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82f31c6e-f9df-5e0a-88a4-a8ccfca00258" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c4ea37-a45d-5542-9544-8258296d9972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286570} {:answer/id #uuid "d25eeda5-2d5b-54f6-8fe0-b6692dd1e6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286571} {:answer/id #uuid "84e7051d-3d50-5942-957f-02499c983754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286572} {:answer/id #uuid "4821ed81-c26f-5644-9c07-8587174e419d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286573} {:answer/id #uuid "237f126f-8cee-5aba-96a2-26794995ea27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4821ed81-c26f-5644-9c07-8587174e419d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286573} :answer-field/id #uuid "95792031-857a-5e51-965a-bd999bb373e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06f467e9-7255-5cf3-8a52-f0bb53fdbe44" :question/math-academy-id "q-146318" :question/problem "The vector $v$ has magnitude $12,$ the vector $w$ has magnitude $10,$ and the angle between the vectors is ${0}^{∘}.$ What is $v\\times w?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are nonzero vectors. Then, $a\\times b=0$ if and only if $a∥b.$\n\nSince the angle between $v$ and $w$ is ${0}^{∘},$ our vectors must be parallel. \n\nTherefore, $v\\times w=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09aeb7f5-31e0-5b2d-9e2a-8eace54a6665" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Vectors Whose Angle Is a Non-Special Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a9b03c2-3795-56d6-b7cb-90d550b08007" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19.81n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a9b03c2-3795-56d6-b7cb-90d550b08007" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19.81n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286577} :answer-field/id #uuid "f494f853-8942-53a9-a642-d8c25a897034" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c180252-ac91-5873-a75b-16560167178b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279282" :question/problem "Given the vector $u$ has magnitude $4$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $5,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${82}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n$ and round your final answer to **two decimal places** where appropriate.\n\n$u\\times v≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =4\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{82}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =20\\cdot (0.990\\,26…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(19.805\\,2…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈19.81n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
